        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-30T14:30:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This case handles zero\u0027ing after a flush from a state change *when* we also happen to reach the end of a buffer (pending ct \u003d\u003d 0), and it handles zero\u0027ing when reach the end of the buffer normally (pending ct \u003e 0), but thinking through possible scenarios, I realized that because we are aligning the start of each suballocation to 4*fStride when pending count \u003d\u003d 0, we need something to zero when there was a flush from a state change too.\n\nI think this can be done pretty simply but having the public `flush()` call `padAndZero()` (and so then newPipelineState and the end of DrawPass::Make go back to normal) and `padAndZero()` is private.  We also have an `internalFlush()` call that `Appender` calls on buffer overflow that doesn\u0027t force zero\u0027ing (since it\u0027ll have manually zero\u0027ed here before the buffer overflowed).  \n\nThis should also let this overflow check be restricted to `fAppendVerts \u0026\u0026 fPendingCount \u003e 0`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 358,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 358,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "8bbcc59b839bc871b7322addcec6451edb296bb9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
